# Duop interface language pack: Українська (Ukrainian).
#
# One "key = value" per line; keys are the LangStrings fields of include/types.inc (English, the
# built-in base, is used for every key a pack leaves out). Values are UTF-8 text; wrap a value in
# "..." to keep leading/trailing spaces. Escapes: \n newline, \t tab, \" quote, \\ backslash.
# {version} expands to the Duop version. Lines starting with # are comments.
#
# Add a language: copy this file to ~/.config/duop/lang/<id>.lang (e.g. de.lang), set `code`
# and `name`, translate the values -- no rebuild. Pick it with --lang <id|code>, `lang = <id>` in
# duoprc, LANG=<id>_XX.UTF-8, or cycle languages with Alt+L.
